{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "strict": true,
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "verbatimModuleSyntax": true,
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["src"],
  // **The WORKER's own file, and only it** (M6.5b). `src/local/worker.ts` is
  // compiled by `tsconfig.worker.json` with `lib: ["ES2022", "WebWorker"]`, and
  // folding it in here would put `DedicatedWorkerGlobalScope` and `document` in
  // one program — each of which is absent where the other is real. Nothing
  // under `src` imports it (the page names it as a URL, which TypeScript does
  // not resolve), so excluding it is enough to keep it out.
  //
  // **`src/local/db.ts` is deliberately NOT listed**, although it is the
  // Worker's too: `src/local/db.test.ts` imports it and runs in jsdom, and an
  // `exclude` does not keep an IMPORTED file out of a program — only out of the
  // root file list. Listing it would read as a fence that is not one. It uses
  // IndexedDB and nothing else, which is in both libs.
  //
  // **The node replay's own file** (M6.5b). `src/local/corpus.node.test.ts`
  // reads `node:fs`, `node:path` and `node:module`, which do not exist in a
  // browser and are not in this project's `types`. It is a ROOT file here — no
  // file under `src` imports it — so excluding it keeps it out, and
  // `tsconfig.node.json` picks it up instead, where `process` and the node
  // module ids are real.
  //
  // **The SERVICE WORKER's own file** (M6.5b2). `src/sw.ts` is compiled by
  // `tsconfig.sw.json` with `lib: ["ES2022", "WebWorker"]` for the same reason
  // the Worker's file is: `clients`, `skipWaiting` and `FetchEvent` are real
  // there and `document` is not. Nothing under `src` imports it — the generator
  // builds it with esbuild — so excluding it is enough to keep it out.
  //
  // **The real-build cell is the node project's** (M6.5b2).
  // `src/precache.node.test.ts` runs a real `vite build` into a temporary
  // directory: it reads `node:fs`, `node:os` and `node:child_process`, and it
  // needs the generated wasm glue that CI's `web-client` job does not build.
  // The `src/local/*.node.test.ts` pattern above does not reach it, so it is
  // named here.
  "exclude": [
    "src/local/worker.ts",
    "src/local/*.node.test.ts",
    "src/sw.ts",
    "src/precache.node.test.ts"
  ]
}
